Stock valuation methods: Method P/E Ratio Forward P/E How to apply Compare the P/E with the industry average. P/E &lt; industry average = 
comparatively cheaper Use the EPS projected for next year. Forward P/E &lt; 20 for growth stock = reasonable PEG Ratio P/E divided by EPS growth rate. PEG &lt; 1 = can be undervalued Price/Free Cash Flow Better than P/E because FCF is difficult to distort. P/FCF &lt; 25 = 
reasonable DCF (Discounted CF) 

